error: List of all unstable flags.
WARNING: these are completely unstable, and may change at any time!

Options:
      -Zui-testing
          Enables UI testing mode

      -Ztrack-diagnostics
          Prints a note for every diagnostic that is emitted with the creation and emission location.
          
          This is enabled by default on debug builds.

      -Zparse-yul
          Enables parsing Yul files for testing

      -Zno-resolve-imports
          Disables import resolution

      -Zrecover-incomplete-input
          Recovers incomplete input into a partial AST

      -Zdump=<KIND[,KIND...][=PATHS...]>
          Print additional information about the compiler's internal state.
          
          Valid kinds are `ast`, `hir`, `mir`, `mir-cfg`, `mir-final`, `evm-ir`, `evm-ir-runtime`, `evm-ir-runtime-scheduled`, `disasm-deploy`, and `disasm-runtime`.

      -Zast-stats
          Print AST stats

      -Zhir-stats
          Print HIR stats

      -Zstandard-json-stats
          Print Standard JSON input stats

      -Zspan-visitor
          Run the span visitor after parsing

      -Zprint-max-storage-sizes
          Print contracts' max storage sizes

      -Zprint-natspec
          Print resolved NatSpec docs as diagnostics for UI tests

      -Zmir-pipeline=<PASS[,PASS...]>
          Comma-separated MIR pass pipeline. Use `default` for the compiler's canonical pipeline and `none` for no passes

      -Zevm-ir-pipeline=<PASS[,PASS...]>
          Comma-separated EVM IR pass pipeline. Use `default` for the compiler's canonical pipeline and `none` for no passes

      -Zprint-after-each
          Print MIR or EVM IR after every optimization pass

      -Zpass-diff
          Print a before-and-after diff for each pass explicitly selected by an IR pipeline

      -Zdebugify=<MODE>
          Audit source debug information after each MIR and EVM IR pass. `report` lists the instructions left without a location and the origins lost; `check` also fails when a pass leaves any instruction without a location, like LLVM's `not-generate` check. Lost origins are information, since deleting code legitimately loses one. Does not change generated code

      -Zdebugify-output=<DIR>
          Write per-pass debug-info audits as JSON lines into this directory. Enables auditing without stderr output; an explicit `-Zdebugify` mode still controls diagnostics

      -Zsolar-tv=<DIR>
          Run solar-tv on changed MIR and EVM IR after each pass. Keep counterexamples and inconclusive pairs in this directory

      -Zvalidate-ir=<BOOL>
          Validate MIR and EVM IR after each pass. Enabled by default in debug builds. Accepts `true` or `false`

      -Ztime-passes
          Print the time spent in each MIR and EVM IR pass

      -Zcodegen-all-functions
          Lower all contract functions instead of only reachable ones. This is intended for benchmarks and compiler debugging

      -Zswitch-lowering <SWITCH_LOWERING>
          Force a switch lowering strategy for benchmarking (default: `auto`; values: `auto`, `linear`, `binary`, `buckets`, `dense`, or `perfect`)

      -Zswitch-max-gas-code-growth <SWITCH_MAX_GAS_CODE_GROWTH>
          Override the artifact-wide bytecode growth budget for gas-optimized switches

      -Zswitch-max-bit-slice-gas-code-growth <SWITCH_MAX_BIT_SLICE_GAS_CODE_GROWTH>
          Override the per-switch bit-slice table growth limit for benchmarking

      -Ztune <TUNE>
          Tune generated code for an execution engine (default: `none`; values: `none`, `interpreter`, `jit`)

      -Zpack-wide-jump-tables
          Pack indexed jump table entries wider than one byte into words and pick them with a shift and a mask. Off by default: jump analysis in bytecode JITs cannot resolve the pick

      -Zcheck-analyses=<BOOL>
          Check every fact MIR optimizations rely on at run time. Enabled by default in debug builds.
          
          Passes record each fact where they act on it, and a violated fact reverts with `AnalysisFactViolated(uint256,uint256,uint256)`. Accepts `true` or `false`; the last one given wins.

      -Zprove-analyses <DIR>
          Write an SMT-LIB query for every fact passes record for `-Zcheck-analyses` to this directory, and record them: Z3 answering `unsat` proves the fact for all inputs, and `sat` gives a counterexample. `-` writes them to stdout. See `tools/prove-analyses`

      -Zvalidate-passes <DIR>
          Write an SMT-LIB query to this directory for every function a MIR pass changes, asking whether some input makes it differ from its version before the pass: Z3 answering `unsat` proves the pass preserved it. `-` writes them to stdout. See `tools/prove-analyses`

      -Zvalidate-backend <DIR>
          Write an SMT-LIB query to this directory for every block of every function stack scheduling lowers, asking whether its scheduled EVM IR can differ from the MIR block when the stack and memory hold the block's values where the schedule says: Z3 answering `unsat` proves the block lowered faithfully. `-` writes them to stdout. See `tools/prove-analyses`

      -Zvalidate-evm-ir-passes <DIR>
          Write an SMT-LIB query to DIR for every code region an EVM IR pass changes, asking whether some state makes it differ from its version before the pass: Z3 answering `unsat` proves the pass preserved it. `-` writes them to stdout. See `tools/prove-analyses`

      -Zvalidate-assembly
          Check the assembled bytecode against the assembly it was solved from: every instruction decodes to its opcode and immediate, every pushed label to the offset of its `JUMPDEST`, and placeholders and program data sit where the artifact records them. A mismatch is an error

      -Zemit-lean-stages <DIR>
          Write the program after every stage of the backend to DIR as Lean definitions of the `solar-tv` semantics, in a directory per contract: the first lowered MIR, the module after each MIR pass that changes it, the scheduled runtime EVM IR, the program after each EVM IR pass that changes it, the runtime bytecode, and a manifest binding them to the sources, the compiler and its options. Code the semantics cannot represent is an error

      -Zhelp
          Print help

Usage: solar [OPTIONS] [INPUT]...

For more information, try '--help'.
